  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building strong development partnerships through our Direct Aid Program 2024-25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Direct Aid Program (DAP) is a small grants program funded by the Australian Government and managed by the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT) overseas Posts. DAP supports Australia&apos;s longer-term country and multilateral development strategies, and the program in Bhutan is committed to relevant, inclusive, and sustainable social and economic development outcomes. The investment will provide targeted funding to local organisations to deliver short-term tangible impact-driven projects that are aligned with Bhutan&#x2019;s Gross National Happiness philosophy, and the Bhutanese Government&#x2019;s 5-year plan.</narrative>
  </description>
